hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1177","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Orouba, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Zurara bin Awfa, on the authority of Saad Ibn Hisham, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “when he prayed a prayer he liked to continue it, and I do not know of a Prophet.” “He, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited the entire Qur’an in one night, and did not get up until the morning, nor did he fast an entire month other than Ramadan.” So I went to Ibn Abbas and told him about her hadith, and he said: She told the truth, but if I were to enter upon her, I would have come to her so that she could tell me about it verbally."
"1178","Ali bin Khashram told us, Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Qatada with this chain of transmission. She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was If he did something, it was proven. She said: “And I have never seen the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stay up all night until the morning, or fast for a consecutive month.” \Except Ramadan\"""""
"1179","Yaqoub Al-Dawraqi told us, Ibn Ulayya told us, H, and Mu’mal bin Hisham told us, Ismail, meaning Ibn Ulayya, told us, on the authority of Uyaynah Ibn Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father, said: Buraydah said: I went out one day walking for a need, and I was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He was walking, and I thought he wanted something, so I started to stop him, and I continued doing that until he saw me, so he pointed to me, so I went to him, and he took my hand. So we all started walking, and we saw a man in front of us who was praying, bowing and prostrating a lot. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do you see? What do you think?” I said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: Then he sent out his hand and applied three passes between his hands. He raised his hands and straightened them, and said: “On you.” “You must guide with intention, upon you is guidance with intent, upon you is guidance with intent; for whoever increases this debt will overcome it.” This is a reliable hadith. Al-Duraqi did not say: Whoever strives for this religion will be defeated by it."
"1180","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, Ibn Ulayya told us, Abdul Aziz bin Suhayb told us, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: The Messenger of God entered May God bless him and grant him peace, there was a rope stretched between two poles, and he said: “What is this?” They said: Zainab prays, but if she is lazy, or if she is lazy, she holds it. He said: “Untie it.” Then he said: “Let one of you pray as he is active, if he is lazy.” Or he gets cold feet, let him sit.”"
"1181","Ibrahim bin Mustamir Al-Basri told us, Abu Habib bin Muslim bin Yahya, the muezzin of the Bani Rifa’ah Mosque, told us Shu’bah, On the authority of Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, something similar, except that he said: They said: Lamimuna bint al-Harith. He said: What do you do with it? They said: She prays standing, and when she becomes tired she relies on it. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, permitted it. He said: “One of you prays when he becomes tired.” let him sit down"
